# BookFlow

This repository is for the XPRTZ code assignment **XPRTZ Code Opdracht 2025**. The assignment describes BookFlow, a platform intended to connect authors, publishers, and distributors and modernize the process from manuscript submission through publication and distribution.

The brief focuses on managing book and manuscript information, coordinating publishing workflows, integrating with external services reliably, sending real-time updates, and building a scalable system with automated tests.

## Original assignment

The original assignment PDF is available at [XPRTZ Code Opdracht 2025.pdf](../XPRTZ%20Code%20Opdracht%202025.pdf).

## Class diagram

The class diagram outlines BookFlow's core domain model. Authors submit manuscripts for editors to review; each manuscript has metadata, version history, highlighted edits, and author feedback. An approved manuscript can become a book published by a publisher, while distributors report book availability through stock records.

```mermaid
classDiagram
	class Author {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class Editor {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class Publisher {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class Manuscript {
		+string Id
		+string Title
		+ManuscriptStatus Status
		+DateTime SubmittedAt
	}
	class ManuscriptVersion {
		+string Id
		+int VersionNumber
		+string BlobUri
		+DateTime CreatedAt
	}
	class ManuscriptMetadata {
		+string Id
	}
	class ManuscriptHighlight {
		+int StartOffset
		+int EndOffset
		+string OriginalText
		+string EditedText
	}
	class AuthorFeedback {
		+string Id
		+string Comment
		+DateTime SubmittedAt
	}
	class Book {
		+string Id
		+string ISBN
		+string Title
	}
	class Distributor {
		+string Id
		+string Name
	}
	class StockRecord {
		+int AvailableQuantity
		+DateTime UpdatedAt
	}

	Author "1" --> "0..*" Manuscript : submits
	Editor "0..1" --> "0..*" Manuscript : reviews
	Manuscript "1" *-- "1" ManuscriptMetadata : metadata
	Manuscript "1" *-- "1..*" ManuscriptVersion : versions
	ManuscriptVersion "1" <-- "0..*" ManuscriptVersion : based on original
	ManuscriptMetadata "1" *-- "0..*" ManuscriptHighlight : stores highlights
	ManuscriptVersion "1" --> "0..*" ManuscriptHighlight : changes in version
	Author "1" --> "0..*" AuthorFeedback : submits
	ManuscriptMetadata "1" *-- "0..*" AuthorFeedback : stores feedback
	ManuscriptVersion "1" --> "0..*" AuthorFeedback : receives response
	Manuscript "1" --> "0..1" Book : approved as
	Publisher "1" --> "0..*" Book : publishes
	Book "1" --> "0..*" StockRecord : availability
	Distributor "1" --> "0..*" StockRecord : reports
```

## New manuscript upload workflow

When an author uploads a manuscript, the Web App stores the file in Blob Storage and manages manuscript and user metadata in SQL Database. Blob Storage sends an upload event to Event Grid, which routes it to the editor-assignment service. The service assigns an editor, saves the assignment, and publishes an `EditorAssigned` event that Event Grid routes to the email service.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Author([Author]) -->|Uploads manuscript| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		BlobStorage[(Blob Storage)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		EditorAssignmentService[Editor assignment service<br/>Assigns an editor]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]

		WebApp -->|Stores manuscript file| BlobStorage
		BlobStorage -->|Manuscript uploaded event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|Routes upload event| EditorAssignmentService
		EditorAssignmentService -->|Persists editor assignment| SqlDatabase
		EditorAssignmentService -->|Publishes EditorAssigned event| EventGrid
		WebApp <-->|Reads and writes manuscript and user metadata| SqlDatabase
	end

	EmailService[Email service]
	Editor([Assigned editor])
	EventGrid -->|Routes EditorAssigned event| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers notification| Editor
```

## Manuscript proofreading workflow

The editor opens the manuscript in the Web App, highlights and edits the text, and saves the result as a new Blob Storage version linked to the original. The Web App stores the highlights and version relationship in SQL Database, then publishes a `ManuscriptEdited` event to Event Grid. Event Grid routes it to an independently deployed author-notification service that looks up the author and updated-version link, then sends an email notification. The author follows the link to read the edited manuscript in the Web App, respond to the changes, and upload a revised version linked to the editor's version. The Web App stores the author's feedback and new version metadata, then publishes a `ManuscriptRevised` event. Event Grid routes that event to an independent editor-notification service, which emails the editor a link to the revised manuscript.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Editor([Editor]) -->|Reviews and highlights manuscript| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		BlobStorage[(Blob Storage)]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		AuthorNotificationService[Author notification service]
		EditorNotificationService[Editor notification service]

		WebApp -->|Loads original manuscript| BlobStorage
		WebApp -->|Stores edited version linked to original| BlobStorage
		WebApp -->|Stores highlights and version metadata| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Publishes ManuscriptEdited event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|Routes ManuscriptEdited event| AuthorNotificationService
		AuthorNotificationService -->|Looks up author and updated-version link| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Stores author feedback and revised-version metadata| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Stores revised version linked to editor's version| BlobStorage
		WebApp -->|Publishes ManuscriptRevised event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|Routes ManuscriptRevised event| EditorNotificationService
		EditorNotificationService -->|Looks up editor and revised-version link| SqlDatabase
	end

	EmailService[Email service]
	Author([Author])
	Editor([Editor])
	AuthorNotificationService -->|Sends email with Web App link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers edited-manuscript notification| Author
	Author -->|Opens updated manuscript link| WebApp
	Author -->|Responds to edits and uploads revision| WebApp
	EditorNotificationService -->|Sends email with revised-manuscript link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers revision notification| Editor
```

## Manuscript approval workflow

When the editor approves a manuscript in the Web App, the approval status is saved in SQL Database and a `ManuscriptApproved` event is published to Event Grid. Event Grid routes the event to independently deployed services: one submits a print demand to the PrintOnDemand API, one emails the author that the manuscript is approved, and one notifies publisher APIs that the new book is available.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Editor([Editor]) -->|Approves manuscript| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		PrintDemandService[Print demand service]
		AuthorApprovalNotificationService[Author approval notification service]
		PublisherAvailabilityService[Publisher availability service]

		WebApp -->|Stores approval status| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Publishes ManuscriptApproved event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|Routes approval event| PrintDemandService
		EventGrid -->|Routes approval event| AuthorApprovalNotificationService
		EventGrid -->|Routes approval event| PublisherAvailabilityService
	end

	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	EmailService[Email service]
	PublisherAPIs[Publisher APIs]
	Author([Author])
	PrintDemandService -->|Requests manuscript printing| PrintOnDemandAPI
	AuthorApprovalNotificationService -->|Sends approval email| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers approval notification| Author
	PublisherAvailabilityService -->|Notifies new book is available| PublisherAPIs
```

## Publisher print order workflow

The publisher uses the Web App to check book availability and requests a print quantity for a selected distributor. The Web App records the order and publishes a `PrintOrderRequested` event to Event Grid. Event Grid routes the event to the print-order service, which submits the title and quantity to the PrintOnDemand API. When the books are delivered, PrintOnDemand publishes a `BooksDelivered` event to Event Grid. The distributor then updates its stock and publishes a `StockUpdated` event. Event Grid routes both events to the inventory service, which updates the stock data used by the Web App.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Publisher([Publisher]) -->|Checks availability and requests print quantity| WebApp

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		WebApp[Web App]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		PrintOrderService[Print order service]
		InventoryService[Inventory service]

		WebApp <-->|Reads book availability| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Stores title, quantity, and distributor| SqlDatabase
		WebApp -->|Publishes PrintOrderRequested event| EventGrid
		EventGrid -->|Routes print order event| PrintOrderService
		EventGrid -->|Routes BooksDelivered and StockUpdated events| InventoryService
		InventoryService -->|Updates stock and availability| SqlDatabase
	end

	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	Distributor([Distributor])
	PrintOrderService -->|Submits title and quantity to print| PrintOnDemandAPI
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|Delivers printed books| Distributor
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|Publishes BooksDelivered event| EventGrid
	Distributor -->|Publishes StockUpdated event| EventGrid
```

## Book production and inventory tracking workflow

The PrintOnDemand API publishes a `BooksPrinted` event with the printed quantity. Distributors publish `BooksDistributed`, `BooksSold`, and `StockUpdated` events as books move through their inventory. Event Grid routes these events to the inventory service, which maintains per-title and per-distributor totals for printed, distributed, and sold books, along with current stock, in SQL Database. The Web App reads these figures for availability and reporting.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API] -->|Publishes BooksPrinted quantity| EventGrid
	Distributor([Distributor]) -->|Publishes BooksDistributed quantity| EventGrid
	Distributor -->|Publishes BooksSold quantity| EventGrid
	Distributor -->|Publishes StockUpdated quantity| EventGrid

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		InventoryService[Inventory service]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		WebApp[Web App]

		EventGrid -->|Routes production, distribution, sales, and stock events| InventoryService
		InventoryService -->|Updates book totals and current stock| SqlDatabase
		WebApp <-->|Reads inventory and sales data| SqlDatabase
	end
```

## Low-stock and reprint decision workflow

When a title reaches 10 books in stock, or its stock reaches 0, the distributor publishes a `LowStockAlert` or `StockDepleted` event to Event Grid. Event Grid routes the events to the inventory service to update SQL stock data and to a publisher-notification service that emails the publisher a link to the Web App. The publisher can review availability and choose whether to request extra copies. A print order is created only if the publisher approves; the print-order service then sends the request to PrintOnDemand for delivery to the distributor.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	Distributor([Distributor]) -->|Stock reaches 10 or 0| EventGrid

	subgraph Azure[Microsoft Azure]
		EventGrid{{Event Grid}}
		InventoryService[Inventory service]
		PublisherNotificationService[Publisher notification service]
		SqlDatabase[(SQL Database)]
		WebApp[Web App]
		ReprintDecision{Print extra copies?}
		PrintOrderService[Print order service]

		EventGrid -->|Routes LowStockAlert and StockDepleted| InventoryService
		InventoryService -->|Updates stock and availability| SqlDatabase
		EventGrid -->|Routes stock alert| PublisherNotificationService
		PublisherNotificationService -->|Looks up publisher and book details| SqlDatabase
		WebApp <-->|Reads current stock and book details| SqlDatabase
		WebApp --> ReprintDecision
		ReprintDecision -->|Yes: stores print order| SqlDatabase
		ReprintDecision -->|Yes: publishes PrintOrderRequested| EventGrid
		ReprintDecision -->|No: no print order| NoReprint([No reprint])
		EventGrid -->|Routes print order| PrintOrderService
	end

	EmailService[Email service]
	Publisher([Publisher])
	PrintOnDemandAPI[PrintOnDemand API]
	PublisherNotificationService -->|Emails Web App link| EmailService
	EmailService -->|Delivers stock alert| Publisher
	Publisher -->|Reviews stock and chooses Yes or No| WebApp
	PrintOrderService -->|Submits title and quantity| PrintOnDemandAPI
	PrintOnDemandAPI -->|Delivers extra copies| Distributor
```

